Evergreen-Patch: firefox-user-agent
Why: Firefox names the browser in its User-Agent after the app basename,
  so Evergreen sent "... Gecko/20100101 Evergreen/157.0" with no Firefox
  token. Sites that look for Firefox then treat Evergreen as another
  browser (addons.mozilla.org says "Download Firefox and get the
  extension" instead of offering to install), and the rare token makes
  Evergreen users easier to fingerprint. Report exactly Firefox's
  User-Agent, as other Firefox-based browsers do. MOZ_APP_UA_NAME can only
  be set by the project's moz.configure.
Upstream: not upstreamable (Firefox itself is named Firefox)
Drop-when: Firefox lets a build set the User-Agent name another way
Owner: Evergreen maintainers

--- a/browser/moz.configure
+++ b/browser/moz.configure
@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@ imply_option("MOZ_PROFILE_MIGRATOR", True)
 
 imply_option("MOZ_APP_VENDOR", "Mozilla")
 imply_option("MOZ_APP_ID", "{ec8030f7-c20a-464f-9b0e-13a3a9e97384}")
+# Evergreen: the same User-Agent as Firefox (see patch header).
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_UA_NAME", "Firefox")
 # Include the DevTools client, not just the server (which is the default)
 imply_option("MOZ_DEVTOOLS", "all")
 imply_option("BROWSER_CHROME_URL", "chrome://browser/content/browser.xhtml")
